  "remarks": "Vadim Vasiliev is the former Deputy Minister of Construction, Housing and Utilities of the Russian Federation, in charge of the Department for the Implementation of Regional Investment Programmes, the Department for Coordination of Socio-Economic Development of Regions and the Department of Social and Economic Development of Certain Territories. He was in charge of implementing the policy of the Ministry of Construction in the annexed regions of Donetsk, Luhansk, Zaporizhzhia and Kherson. Subsidies from the federal budget of the Russian Government are channelled through the Ministry of Construction in order to strengthen the “redevelopment” of the Ukrainian regions currently under Russian control. Currently, he is the director of the Department of Regional Development of Russia, which is part of the Ministry of Economic Development of the Russian Federation. Therefore, he is still a member of the Russian government.",
